1
00:00:04,667 --> 00:00:11,633
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,467 --> 00:00:32,600
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:34,900
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:41,067
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,667
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:44,900
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,033 --> 00:00:46,067
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,667 --> 00:00:48,400
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:49,933 --> 00:00:51,000
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:53,367
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:55,267
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,433 --> 00:00:57,700
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:57,833 --> 00:01:00,200
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:00,833 --> 00:01:03,000
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:06,267
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,033 --> 00:01:09,067
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:09,967 --> 00:01:11,400
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,533 --> 00:01:12,600
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:12,733 --> 00:01:14,500
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,633 --> 00:01:21,033
<i>How could you mess up again,
Lucas?!</i>

21
00:01:21,167 --> 00:01:22,133
<i> I had to save you!</i>

22
00:01:22,267 --> 00:01:24,700
<i>Our mission was
to get Victor back.</i>

23
00:01:24,833 --> 00:01:28,433
<i>Now, because of your meddling,
your brother will rot in prison!</i>

24
00:01:28,567 --> 00:01:30,433
<i>- Argh!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

25
00:01:30,567 --> 00:01:32,633
<i>Despite the attack, we were
still able to transfer Victor</i>

26
00:01:32,767 --> 00:01:34,700
<i>to maximum security.
Good job, team.</i>

27
00:01:34,833 --> 00:01:36,567
<i> We saved the NCIA.</i>

28
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:38,800
<i>NLEA are the heroes here.
Do you understand?</i>

29
00:01:38,933 --> 00:01:40,133
<i> Mission accomplished, General.</i>

30
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:42,567
<i>Have you forgotten that
my daughter is still missing?</i>

31
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:45,233
<i>Until you find her,
you can't rest.</i>

32
00:01:45,367 --> 00:01:47,567
<i>We wanted to talk
to Samantha Jacinto</i>

33
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:49,433
<i>about the progress
of Zafra's case.</i>

34
00:01:49,567 --> 00:01:51,133
<i>But, sir,
they said she isn't here.</i>

35
00:01:51,267 --> 00:01:52,967
<i> It's true. She's on leave.</i>

36
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:55,167
<i>- Badong fell off the roof.
- [BODY THUDS]</i>

37
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:56,567
<i>He needs to lay down
on something.</i>

38
00:01:56,700 --> 00:01:58,033
<i> One, two, three, roll.</i>

39
00:01:58,167 --> 00:01:59,867
<i>Put his head in front.
Be careful now!</i>

40
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,133
<i>Come on, get inside.
It's not safe!</i>

41
00:02:01,267 --> 00:02:03,633
<i>I saw the men who were
looking for her last night.</i>

42
00:02:03,767 --> 00:02:05,067
<i>I saw them
while I was buying food.</i>

43
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:07,333
<i>Didn't you already ask people
to be our lookouts?</i>

44
00:02:07,467 --> 00:02:09,467
<i>Yes, Pa. We've got people
stationed in the alleys.</i>

45
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:11,900
<i> We can't let Gloria out.</i>

46
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:14,167
[MARIANO SIGHS DEEPLY]

47
00:02:14,333 --> 00:02:17,433
- Sir, your wound.
- This is nothing.

48
00:02:18,533 --> 00:02:19,467
[MARIANO EXHALES]

49
00:02:21,767 --> 00:02:23,567
What exactly happened?

50
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:26,033
I thought everything
was well planned?

51
00:02:26,167 --> 00:02:28,633
Your son let his emotions
get the better of him.

52
00:02:28,767 --> 00:02:30,233
He wasn't thinking!

53
00:02:30,367 --> 00:02:31,733
How can you trust him
with the business

54
00:02:31,867 --> 00:02:33,200
when he acts like that?!

55
00:02:33,333 --> 00:02:36,967
- Arturo, call our doctor.
- [ARTURO] Yes, ma'am.

56
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:40,867
- I don't need a doctor!
- You're too stubborn!

57
00:02:50,367 --> 00:02:51,767
[LINE RINGS]

58
00:02:52,567 --> 00:02:56,500
Hello? I would like
to have my office checked.

59
00:02:56,633 --> 00:03:00,267
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

60
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:02,833
It seems like they know...

61
00:03:03,767 --> 00:03:06,133
...our moves
before we even get to act.

62
00:03:06,267 --> 00:03:10,200
Check to see if there is
a listening device...

63
00:03:10,933 --> 00:03:16,533
...a transmitter, or anything
that shouldn't be here.

64
00:03:16,667 --> 00:03:19,333
No one should know about this.

65
00:03:20,667 --> 00:03:21,833
Did you find anything?

66
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:24,933
It's clear, sir.
There are no bugs.

67
00:03:25,767 --> 00:03:28,267
Check the conference room next.

68
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:32,167
Then make a sweep
of the entire office.

69
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:33,433
- [AGENT 1] Yes, sir.
- [AGENT 2] Yes, sir.

70
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:35,233
Let's move this.

71
00:03:35,367 --> 00:03:37,300
[LADDER CLATTERING]

72
00:03:38,700 --> 00:03:39,867
- [TOOL BOX LID SHUTS]
- [OBJECTS THUD]

73
00:03:44,367 --> 00:03:45,600
- [DELGADO SIGHS]
- Sir.

74
00:03:47,133 --> 00:03:48,133
What was that for?

75
00:03:51,100 --> 00:03:52,667
I'm just making sure.

76
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:56,267
I mean, I can't figure out why

77
00:03:56,433 --> 00:04:01,233
the Zafras know our movements.

78
00:04:01,367 --> 00:04:03,267
It's either we're being bugged,

79
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:07,533
or they have an insider
within the NCIA.

80
00:04:07,667 --> 00:04:12,133
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

81
00:04:12,267 --> 00:04:16,267
The Zafras have an insider
within the NCIA?

82
00:04:20,433 --> 00:04:22,800
[PIA] I think--
I think that's impossible.

83
00:04:22,933 --> 00:04:23,967
[PIA CHUCKLES AIRILY]

84
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:26,367
You know, sir, I think

85
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:31,033
Team Alpha just failed
this very simple mission.

86
00:04:31,833 --> 00:04:33,400
Pia, given the size
of the business

87
00:04:33,533 --> 00:04:35,800
and the amount of money
the Zafras have,

88
00:04:35,933 --> 00:04:39,133
they can buy
not only information,

89
00:04:39,267 --> 00:04:41,100
but also people.

90
00:04:42,467 --> 00:04:44,200
[CLEARS THROAT] Alright, if--

91
00:04:45,267 --> 00:04:47,200
If we do have a traitor
in the NCIA...

92
00:04:47,967 --> 00:04:50,967
I'll investigate it.

93
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:52,300
Please do, Pia.

94
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:54,900
You are the police officer
in NCIA.

95
00:04:55,500 --> 00:05:00,667
Find out who the traitor is
in our agency.

96
00:05:04,433 --> 00:05:08,200
- Karen, is there a problem?
- What do you think?

97
00:05:08,900 --> 00:05:11,500
I know you're worried about Sam
'cause you're close friends,

98
00:05:11,633 --> 00:05:15,200
but we haven't stopped
searching for her.

99
00:05:16,133 --> 00:05:17,900
Do those guys look worried?

100
00:05:18,033 --> 00:05:19,833
- You?
- Of course!

101
00:05:19,967 --> 00:05:22,367
Wait, what are you thinking?

102
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:26,000
I would only trust people
who truly care about Sam.

103
00:05:26,133 --> 00:05:29,667
And even if I want to know
what's on your minds,

104
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:31,000
that's impossible.

105
00:05:31,133 --> 00:05:34,500
So, next time, don't ask me
what I'm thinking, okay?

106
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:36,300
[KAREN SIGHS]

107
00:05:36,433 --> 00:05:37,933
[INDISTINCT CONVERSATION]

108
00:05:38,067 --> 00:05:39,400
Karen, what are you doing?

109
00:05:39,967 --> 00:05:41,367
- Karen!
- Guys.

110
00:05:41,900 --> 00:05:44,633
- How can you do this?
- What?

111
00:05:44,767 --> 00:05:48,533
You just chatting
and focusing on your work,

112
00:05:48,667 --> 00:05:50,533
as if Sam isn't missing.

113
00:05:50,667 --> 00:05:52,033
Come on, Karen.
What are you?

114
00:05:52,533 --> 00:05:54,267
I think about her all the time.

115
00:05:54,400 --> 00:05:57,500
Me too, Karen.
And I'm sure we all are.

116
00:06:02,367 --> 00:06:04,067
Will we be able to find Sam?

117
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:06,633
Karen, what kind of question
is that?

118
00:06:07,233 --> 00:06:08,433
Of course.

119
00:06:09,500 --> 00:06:11,100
Look at them.

120
00:06:11,933 --> 00:06:13,000
Look at me.

121
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:15,967
All of the best agents
are looking for Sam.

122
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:19,000
[RALLOS] Guys, just try
to understand Karen.

123
00:06:19,133 --> 00:06:21,700
She treats Ma'am Sam
like family.

124
00:06:21,833 --> 00:06:24,867
You know, Karen,
don't worry too much.

125
00:06:25,367 --> 00:06:27,600
We're going to find Sam.

126
00:06:27,933 --> 00:06:29,400
Don't lose hope.

127
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:31,800
Until we do,

128
00:06:31,933 --> 00:06:34,400
I hope she's safe.

129
00:06:36,667 --> 00:06:37,667
[PLATES CLATTERING]

130
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:39,100
Dear...

131
00:06:40,233 --> 00:06:42,433
There's still a bit of grease.
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

132
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:44,833
Would you like
to switch places?

133
00:06:44,967 --> 00:06:46,033
I'll handle it.

134
00:06:46,367 --> 00:06:48,267
- Just stack them, alright?
- Okay.

135
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:49,400
Alright then.

136
00:06:50,033 --> 00:06:52,100
[MAMENG] Oh my, my, my...

137
00:06:52,233 --> 00:06:54,600
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

138
00:06:54,733 --> 00:06:56,600
- Still a bit greasy.
- [CHUCKLES] Yeah...

139
00:06:56,733 --> 00:06:58,233
- I'm sorry.
- No worries.

140
00:06:58,367 --> 00:06:59,433
Uh...

141
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:03,833
You know, I've noticed that...

142
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:06,167
your hands look so nice.

143
00:07:06,533 --> 00:07:09,067
They look so smooth.

144
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:10,933
You must be rich.

145
00:07:11,067 --> 00:07:13,333
You must have had a good life,

146
00:07:13,467 --> 00:07:15,367
been raised in comfort.

147
00:07:16,033 --> 00:07:17,233
- Uh...
- [WATER SPLASHING]

148
00:07:17,367 --> 00:07:18,600
I wouldn't know.

149
00:07:18,733 --> 00:07:20,233
It really shows.

150
00:07:20,367 --> 00:07:22,633
Plus, you don't even know
how to wash plates.

151
00:07:22,767 --> 00:07:23,633
[CHUCKLES]

152
00:07:23,767 --> 00:07:24,767
But that's okay.

153
00:07:24,900 --> 00:07:25,767
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

154
00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:26,767
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

155
00:07:26,900 --> 00:07:29,267
I'm sorry.
I don't remember anything.

156
00:07:31,767 --> 00:07:33,267
You know, I was thinking...

157
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:34,767
[WATER SPLASHING]

158
00:07:34,900 --> 00:07:36,900
How did Gabo and I
end up together?

159
00:07:37,967 --> 00:07:41,533
Oh, he already told you
the story, right?

160
00:07:41,667 --> 00:07:44,867
Didn't you meet in prison?

161
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,533
That's where you fell in love,

162
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:49,433
exchanged letters,

163
00:07:49,567 --> 00:07:51,200
and later got married.

164
00:07:51,333 --> 00:07:52,333
Honestly, I have no idea

165
00:07:52,467 --> 00:07:55,700
why he didn't mention it
to us when he was released.

166
00:07:55,833 --> 00:07:57,067
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

167
00:07:57,200 --> 00:07:58,233
[SIGHS]

168
00:07:58,367 --> 00:07:59,400
[DIDAY] Gabo!

169
00:07:59,967 --> 00:08:02,633
You're lucky to have
a nice woman in your life.

170
00:08:02,767 --> 00:08:05,767
Imagine, Gloria sat with us
and had a few drinks.

171
00:08:06,300 --> 00:08:09,200
She knows how to blend in
and get along.

172
00:08:09,333 --> 00:08:11,633
Come on, Ma. She only drank
because you asked her to.

173
00:08:11,767 --> 00:08:12,767
It's not like that!

174
00:08:12,900 --> 00:08:15,067
Can you imagine? A beautiful
woman doing all that.

175
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:16,700
You're lucky, Gabo.

176
00:08:16,833 --> 00:08:19,133
Well, you're lucky
to have me too, Diday, right?

177
00:08:19,267 --> 00:08:22,867
Hey! Even if I'm drunk,
don't mess with me!

178
00:08:23,267 --> 00:08:24,667
You're not handsome in my eyes!

179
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:26,000
- You're ugly!
- Ma...

180
00:08:26,133 --> 00:08:27,333
[DANTE CHUCKLES]

181
00:08:27,567 --> 00:08:28,533
Elton!

182
00:08:29,367 --> 00:08:30,367
Hey.

183
00:08:30,967 --> 00:08:32,867
Elton, how is Badong?

184
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,000
Badong is fine.

185
00:08:34,133 --> 00:08:36,633
His family is there,
watching over him.

186
00:08:36,767 --> 00:08:38,267
[RUDY]
So, was his injury bad?

187
00:08:38,400 --> 00:08:40,367
He had a cut on his head,
but it's already stitched up.

188
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:42,100
And before even got
to the hospital,

189
00:08:42,233 --> 00:08:43,267
he was already conscious.

190
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:45,000
[GABO]
That's good, Mister Elton.

191
00:08:45,133 --> 00:08:47,167
At least it wasn't too serious.

192
00:08:47,300 --> 00:08:51,100
[ELTON] I think he'll be home
in a few days.

193
00:08:51,233 --> 00:08:52,467
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

194
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:53,600
[ELTON] By the way, Gabo...

195
00:08:53,733 --> 00:08:56,000
You know, we're all really
impressed with your wife.

196
00:08:56,167 --> 00:08:57,800
- She was amazing.
- Seriously.

197
00:08:57,933 --> 00:08:59,367
You know why?

198
00:08:59,500 --> 00:09:01,900
Gloria was the first
to help Badong.

199
00:09:02,567 --> 00:09:04,133
- Yes, she helped him.
- Exactly.

200
00:09:04,267 --> 00:09:05,633
- It's true.
- Like an angel.

201
00:09:05,767 --> 00:09:08,100
[ELTON] If we carried
Badong without care,

202
00:09:08,233 --> 00:09:10,700
his back might've been hurt.

203
00:09:10,833 --> 00:09:12,533
Yes, Gloria is awesome!

204
00:09:12,667 --> 00:09:14,000
You're lucky, Gabo.

205
00:09:14,133 --> 00:09:16,267
- I agree, Gabo!
- That's right!

206
00:09:16,400 --> 00:09:18,133
- She's been a great help.
- [DIDAY] Yes, that's true!

207
00:09:18,267 --> 00:09:19,800
- A lifesaver!
- Beautiful, with a purpose!

208
00:09:20,633 --> 00:09:21,500
[SAM] I'm so sorry.

209
00:09:21,633 --> 00:09:23,267
I just feel so lost.

210
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:25,167
[WATER SPLASHING]

211
00:09:25,300 --> 00:09:28,833
It's hard for me
to trust what Gabo says.

212
00:09:29,467 --> 00:09:31,167
[MAMENG] Oh no, dear...

213
00:09:32,233 --> 00:09:34,433
You have to trust Gabo.

214
00:09:34,567 --> 00:09:37,567
You know, he's a genuinely
kind man.

215
00:09:37,700 --> 00:09:39,733
I should know.

216
00:09:39,867 --> 00:09:43,433
That's why
he's so protective of you.

217
00:09:43,567 --> 00:09:45,100
He's a good person.

218
00:09:45,433 --> 00:09:46,433
Hmm?

219
00:09:47,733 --> 00:09:49,767
- [PLATES RATTLING]
- [WATER SPLASHING]

220
00:09:49,900 --> 00:09:51,100
[SAM] I hope so.

221
00:09:51,700 --> 00:09:54,100
<i> But the way I know Gabo,</i>

222
00:09:55,067 --> 00:09:56,533
<i> he seems completely different.</i>

223
00:09:57,433 --> 00:10:00,067
<i>I hope to uncover
who he really is soon.</i>

224
00:10:02,300 --> 00:10:02,900
[DOOR OPENS]

225
00:10:02,900 --> 00:10:09,467
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

226
00:10:09,467 --> 00:10:10,467
[GROANS]

227
00:10:10,467 --> 00:10:12,300
[DEBORAH]
With this happening,

228
00:10:12,300 --> 00:10:13,867
I'm sure...

229
00:10:14,367 --> 00:10:17,300
...security around Victor
will tighten,

230
00:10:17,300 --> 00:10:19,700
and I doubt
we'll ever have a chance

231
00:10:19,700 --> 00:10:22,200
to visit him again,
wherever he was taken.

232
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:24,467
It was all Lucas' fault.

233
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:26,667
Why did you even
make him follow me?

234
00:10:26,667 --> 00:10:28,067
Don't you trust me?

235
00:10:28,067 --> 00:10:31,433
I said I just wanted
to make sure!

236
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,100
[MARIANO SIGHS LOUDLY]

237
00:10:33,100 --> 00:10:38,367
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

238
00:10:38,400 --> 00:10:39,400
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

239
00:10:41,633 --> 00:10:44,400
Our business is crippled
while Victor is gone.

240
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:46,367
And that was our only chance.

241
00:10:46,700 --> 00:10:49,800
You placed too much faith
in your son's abilities.

242
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:51,200
Now look at the consequences.

243
00:10:51,533 --> 00:10:53,100
You went so far as to boast

244
00:10:53,100 --> 00:10:55,500
about what Lucas did
to Samantha Jacinto,

245
00:10:55,500 --> 00:10:58,233
but we're not even sure
if she's dead yet!

246
00:10:58,233 --> 00:11:03,733
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

247
00:11:03,733 --> 00:11:05,633
[FOOTSTEPS RECEDING]

248
00:11:05,633 --> 00:11:06,833
[DOOR OPENS]

249
00:11:11,767 --> 00:11:13,167
Here's the latest report
submitted....

250
00:11:13,167 --> 00:11:14,600
Karen, come here.

251
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:15,667
- He's here.
- Tony.

252
00:11:15,667 --> 00:11:17,167
- Sir.
- Uh...

253
00:11:17,667 --> 00:11:19,900
Come with me to Soriano Street.

254
00:11:19,900 --> 00:11:23,967
Maybe the last agents who went
there missed some details.

255
00:11:23,967 --> 00:11:28,900
Robert and Bullet,
check the hospitals and clinics.

256
00:11:28,900 --> 00:11:32,500
And James,
consolidate the new leads.

257
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:33,567
Yes, sir.

258
00:11:33,567 --> 00:11:35,933
[RALLOS] Uh, sir,
what about me, sir?

259
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:37,900
Stay close to Sir Delgado

260
00:11:37,900 --> 00:11:39,200
and update me

261
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:41,133
when you hear
anything new from him.

262
00:11:41,500 --> 00:11:42,633
[RALLOS] Copy, sir.

263
00:11:42,633 --> 00:11:44,133
Sir, when are we leaving?

264
00:11:44,133 --> 00:11:45,133
Right now.

265
00:11:45,133 --> 00:11:46,533
We can't waste time. Let's go.

266
00:11:46,533 --> 00:11:48,500
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

267
00:11:48,500 --> 00:11:49,733
Take care.

268
00:11:49,733 --> 00:11:52,633
If the National Law Enforcement
Agency had not arrived,

269
00:11:52,633 --> 00:11:55,600
Victor Zafra, alias Tiger,
would have escaped.

270
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:57,200
What happened was clear.

271
00:11:57,200 --> 00:12:00,200
The NCIA has lacked in security,

272
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:02,500
and we were the ones
who cleaned up after them.

273
00:12:06,133 --> 00:12:07,733
- Ah, sir?
- Yes?

274
00:12:07,733 --> 00:12:09,000
Do you need anything?

275
00:12:10,233 --> 00:12:12,433
Not really.
Why did you ask?

276
00:12:12,733 --> 00:12:14,533
Uh, sir, I thought
you called for--

277
00:12:14,567 --> 00:12:16,467
- [PIA] Sir?
- [DELGADO] Yes?

278
00:12:16,467 --> 00:12:18,767
Sir, the NLEA is holding
a press conference

279
00:12:18,767 --> 00:12:20,367
and it's being live-streamed.

280
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:24,967
As a result of the swift action
<i> taken by the NLEA,</i>

281
00:12:24,967 --> 00:12:30,000
high-value detainee Victor Zafra
<i> was successfully transferred</i>

282
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:33,567
to a maximum-security
detention facility.

283
00:12:33,567 --> 00:12:35,100
[REPORTER 1]
Sir, just a follow-up question.

284
00:12:35,100 --> 00:12:37,167
- Ma'am, that's enough for now.
- Just one more question!

285
00:12:37,167 --> 00:12:38,300
- Sir, let's go.
- [REPORTER 2] Sir! Sir!

286
00:12:38,300 --> 00:12:41,367
- Just a quick question!
- Last follow-up, sir!

287
00:12:41,367 --> 00:12:43,167
Geez! Way to hog the spot--

288
00:12:43,167 --> 00:12:45,067
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

289
00:12:45,067 --> 00:12:46,733
Sir, what are you going
to do now?

290
00:12:47,067 --> 00:12:48,700
- Ernesto.
- Sir?

291
00:12:48,733 --> 00:12:50,633
Tell the driver
to prepare the car.

292
00:12:50,633 --> 00:12:51,667
Yes, sir.

293
00:12:52,700 --> 00:12:53,800
Excuse me.

294
00:12:59,600 --> 00:13:01,033
- [DOOR OPENS]
- Unbelievable, man.

295
00:13:01,033 --> 00:13:03,533
I thought you were about
call out the Jacintos again.

296
00:13:03,533 --> 00:13:04,633
[CAMERA THUDS]

297
00:13:04,633 --> 00:13:05,900
- [DOOR CLOSES]
- Come on.

298
00:13:06,233 --> 00:13:07,633
There are still plenty
of chances.

299
00:13:07,633 --> 00:13:09,100
He's got a lot of dirt.

300
00:13:09,467 --> 00:13:11,767
Maybe not just
General Jacinto himself.

301
00:13:11,767 --> 00:13:13,600
Maybe even his entire family.

302
00:13:13,867 --> 00:13:16,667
The problem is,
Boss Arnel is counting on us

303
00:13:16,667 --> 00:13:19,500
to nail General Jacinto!

304
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:22,267
- [SIGHS]
- [ARNEL] Salvador!

305
00:13:22,267 --> 00:13:23,500
What happened?!

306
00:13:23,500 --> 00:13:25,900
They said Jacinto is
on leave, boss.

307
00:13:25,900 --> 00:13:27,067
On leave?

308
00:13:27,500 --> 00:13:29,867
Or just hiding from you?

309
00:13:29,867 --> 00:13:31,100
Watch this.

310
00:13:31,300 --> 00:13:35,033
If the National Law Enforcement
<i> Agency had not arrived,</i>

311
00:13:35,033 --> 00:13:38,567
<i> Victor Zafra, alias Tiger,
would have escaped.</i>

312
00:13:38,567 --> 00:13:41,233
As a result of the swift action
<i> taken by the NLEA,</i>

313
00:13:41,867 --> 00:13:46,467
high-value detainee Victor Zafra
<i> was successfully transferred</i>

314
00:13:46,467 --> 00:13:50,167
<i>to a maximum-security
detention facility.</i>

315
00:13:50,167 --> 00:13:51,467
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

316
00:13:51,467 --> 00:13:54,167
Tomorrow, I want you
to go to the NLEA!

317
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:55,800
Dig into this!

318
00:13:55,800 --> 00:13:57,900
Use your star power, Salvador!

319
00:13:57,900 --> 00:13:58,900
[SALVADOR CLEARS THROAT]

320
00:13:58,900 --> 00:14:01,800
Dude, looks like the NLEA is
still your way

321
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:03,300
to General Jacinto.

322
00:14:03,733 --> 00:14:04,733
Yeah, seems that way.

323
00:14:04,733 --> 00:14:06,333
The NLEA really is
the key, right?

324
00:14:06,333 --> 00:14:08,133
[OLI] Well, if that's the story,
why not?

325
00:14:08,133 --> 00:14:10,800
We'll include that
in the next episode.

326
00:14:11,133 --> 00:14:12,400
Sure, whatever.

327
00:14:13,233 --> 00:14:15,133
For the sake of truth.

328
00:14:15,133 --> 00:14:16,200
No.

329
00:14:16,933 --> 00:14:19,200
For the sake of the ratings!

330
00:14:19,533 --> 00:14:21,767
- [FOOTSTEPS RECEDING]
- [DOOR OPENS]

331
00:14:21,767 --> 00:14:22,867
[DOOR OPENS]

332
00:14:22,867 --> 00:14:26,867
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

333
00:14:26,867 --> 00:14:28,833
[DEBORAH SIGHS]

334
00:14:30,400 --> 00:14:31,633
Lucas.

335
00:14:32,300 --> 00:14:33,367
[LUCAS SIGHS]

336
00:14:33,367 --> 00:14:34,933
I messed up, Ma.

337
00:14:35,867 --> 00:14:37,567
I'm useless.

338
00:14:37,567 --> 00:14:38,467
[DEBORAH EXHALES]

339
00:14:38,900 --> 00:14:39,967
Papa is right.

340
00:14:41,500 --> 00:14:43,167
I'm not like my brother.

341
00:14:43,467 --> 00:14:45,767
Don't be too hard on yourself.

342
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,133
Ma...

343
00:14:49,167 --> 00:14:51,133
What will happen now
to my brother?

344
00:14:52,900 --> 00:14:55,933
Looks like he will be in prison
for a long time.

345
00:14:58,333 --> 00:14:59,867
Since my brother is
not around, Ma...

346
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:03,133
I'll finish what he started.

347
00:15:03,967 --> 00:15:06,200
We already had our revenge
on Samantha Jacinto.

348
00:15:07,133 --> 00:15:10,000
My next target is the guy
she fought with in Chinatown.

349
00:15:15,133 --> 00:15:16,233
[MUSIC FADES]

350
00:15:16,233 --> 00:15:17,733
- Rudy?
- Hmm?

351
00:15:17,733 --> 00:15:19,733
Isn't it your birthday tomorrow?
What's the plan?

352
00:15:19,733 --> 00:15:21,033
[LIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

353
00:15:21,033 --> 00:15:22,133
I don't have plans.

354
00:15:22,133 --> 00:15:24,133
That's the least
of my priorities.

355
00:15:24,133 --> 00:15:26,967
I don't have money to spend
on food and drinks.

356
00:15:26,967 --> 00:15:28,333
Come on, Rudy.

357
00:15:28,333 --> 00:15:30,733
You're no stranger!
Alcohol is on me!

358
00:15:30,733 --> 00:15:31,767
- Nice!
- Nice!

359
00:15:31,767 --> 00:15:34,733
- Uncle Rudy, barchow's on us.
- [MEN] Nice!

360
00:15:34,767 --> 00:15:36,700
I'll cook stir-fry noodles!

361
00:15:36,700 --> 00:15:38,067
[MEN] Nice!

362
00:15:38,067 --> 00:15:39,767
I appreciate it
but you don't have to.

363
00:15:39,767 --> 00:15:41,067
It's a lot of trouble.

364
00:15:41,067 --> 00:15:42,567
I'm old, folks.

365
00:15:42,567 --> 00:15:44,500
I don't celebrate
birthdays anymore.

366
00:15:44,500 --> 00:15:45,900
Rudy,

367
00:15:45,900 --> 00:15:48,667
- you should be grateful.
- [MUSIC TURNS SOFT]

368
00:15:48,667 --> 00:15:49,700
Think about it,

369
00:15:49,700 --> 00:15:53,100
Jacinto tried to force us
out of our homes.

370
00:15:53,100 --> 00:15:54,567
And you've even been shot.

371
00:15:54,567 --> 00:15:56,700
Look at you still alive today.

372
00:15:56,700 --> 00:15:59,800
You should be grateful to God.

373
00:15:59,800 --> 00:16:01,900
- You're so stubborn.
- Rudy.

374
00:16:01,900 --> 00:16:04,600
It's your birthday. Of course,
we should celebrate.

375
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:06,833
Don't worry about it.
We'll all chip in, right?

376
00:16:06,833 --> 00:16:07,933
[ALL] Yes!

377
00:16:07,933 --> 00:16:09,633
We should celebrate.

378
00:16:09,667 --> 00:16:11,767
- Right!
- You're right!

379
00:16:12,633 --> 00:16:16,533
Pa, Auntie Diday
and Uncle Elton are right.

380
00:16:16,533 --> 00:16:19,033
You should definitely celebrate
your birthday.

381
00:16:19,033 --> 00:16:20,367
Don't worry.

382
00:16:20,367 --> 00:16:23,233
We'll work it out so we can
celebrate your birthday.

383
00:16:23,233 --> 00:16:24,333
[ALL] Nice!

384
00:16:24,333 --> 00:16:25,367
Okay, hep-hep!

385
00:16:25,367 --> 00:16:26,733
- Hurray!
- Hurray!

386
00:16:26,733 --> 00:16:27,867
[CHEERING, APPLAUSE]

387
00:16:27,867 --> 00:16:29,667
Thank you! Thank you, folks!

388
00:16:29,667 --> 00:16:31,633
Oh. [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

389
00:16:31,633 --> 00:16:33,833
They seem to be
having fun out there.

390
00:16:35,333 --> 00:16:37,367
Is it always like this in here?

391
00:16:37,367 --> 00:16:39,333
Why? Are they too loud?

392
00:16:39,333 --> 00:16:40,933
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY] Not really.

393
00:16:40,933 --> 00:16:42,867
I'm not just used to it.

394
00:16:42,900 --> 00:16:44,000
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY] Oh.

395
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:46,667
Don't worry, you will be.

396
00:16:46,667 --> 00:16:50,500
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

397
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:52,567
- [SAM]<i> This is my chance.
</i>- [MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

398
00:16:52,567 --> 00:16:54,533
<i>This is my window
while they're all busy.</i>

399
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:00,467
Uh, can I go back
inside the room to rest?

400
00:17:00,467 --> 00:17:02,100
Of course.

401
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:04,033
Go on, dear. Get some rest.

402
00:17:04,033 --> 00:17:05,100
Okay.

403
00:17:05,100 --> 00:17:06,767
Thanks for helping.

404
00:17:21,867 --> 00:17:28,833
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

405
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:33,000
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

406
00:17:33,133 --> 00:17:34,200
- Good evening.
- Good evening.

407
00:17:34,333 --> 00:17:36,667
We need to talk
to Colonel Romulo Domingo.

408
00:17:36,800 --> 00:17:37,633
Can I get your names?

409
00:17:37,767 --> 00:17:40,000
Chief Fernando Delgado of NCIA.

410
00:17:40,133 --> 00:17:41,867
Alright, sir.
You can come upstairs.

411
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:43,000
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

412
00:17:43,367 --> 00:17:45,200
Men, remember,

413
00:17:45,333 --> 00:17:48,233
24/7 surveillance
in Soriano Street.

414
00:17:49,633 --> 00:17:50,467
Understood?

415
00:17:50,600 --> 00:17:51,467
- Yes, ma'am!
- Yes, ma'am!

416
00:17:51,600 --> 00:17:52,700
Go!

417
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:56,267
Max.

418
00:17:58,133 --> 00:18:00,567
We'll come with you tomorrow
to find your sister.

419
00:18:00,700 --> 00:18:02,800
There's no need for that.
We got this.

420
00:18:02,933 --> 00:18:06,433
Oh, come on.
Did you hear I was a hero today?

421
00:18:06,567 --> 00:18:07,433
Really?

422
00:18:07,567 --> 00:18:08,567
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

423
00:18:08,700 --> 00:18:10,433
Your father gave us an order.

424
00:18:10,567 --> 00:18:12,733
And we executed it smoothly.

425
00:18:12,867 --> 00:18:15,900
We moved Victor Zafra
to maximum security.

426
00:18:16,033 --> 00:18:17,733
The Victor Zafra case

427
00:18:17,867 --> 00:18:19,767
was the last case
your sister handled.

428
00:18:21,867 --> 00:18:23,167
Where's Domingo?

429
00:18:27,200 --> 00:18:28,233
Sir.

430
00:18:31,600 --> 00:18:33,000
Fernando.

431
00:18:33,133 --> 00:18:35,200
Romulo, we need to talk.

432
00:18:35,333 --> 00:18:36,467
My office.

433
00:18:37,267 --> 00:18:40,333
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

434
00:18:42,833 --> 00:18:44,800
Please have a seat, Fernando.

435
00:18:44,933 --> 00:18:47,067
Victor Zafra's case is ongoing.

436
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:49,267
Why did you let the press
know about this now?

437
00:18:51,333 --> 00:18:55,167
I'm sorry if you feel offended
that I'm proud of NLEA.

438
00:18:55,333 --> 00:18:58,267
You made it sound like
we fell short.

439
00:18:58,400 --> 00:19:00,067
And you came in to save the day.

440
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:02,167
If not for my men,

441
00:19:02,300 --> 00:19:03,900
Victor Zafra would've escaped.

442
00:19:04,033 --> 00:19:07,133
My agents were competent
and capable.

443
00:19:07,267 --> 00:19:08,833
Your job is reinforcement.

444
00:19:08,967 --> 00:19:12,200
You made it sound like you were
the hero in that operation.

445
00:19:12,333 --> 00:19:15,733
For what?
To improve NLEA's public image?

446
00:19:16,600 --> 00:19:17,700
Fine.

447
00:19:17,833 --> 00:19:20,033
I admit there was
a lapse in my judgment.

448
00:19:20,167 --> 00:19:21,800
But you also have to admit

449
00:19:21,933 --> 00:19:25,900
that NLEA made huge efforts
with regard to the transfer.

450
00:19:26,033 --> 00:19:27,433
Okay, thank you for that.

451
00:19:27,567 --> 00:19:29,000
But we will take it from here.

452
00:19:29,167 --> 00:19:30,767
- I can't do that.
- Why?

453
00:19:30,900 --> 00:19:34,233
We've received a direct order
from General Jacinto.

454
00:19:34,367 --> 00:19:36,000
We've formed a task force

455
00:19:36,133 --> 00:19:39,267
to find your missing agent.

456
00:19:41,133 --> 00:19:43,200
Fernando, don't you think
it'll be quicker

457
00:19:43,333 --> 00:19:45,467
if we both act on it?

458
00:19:45,600 --> 00:19:46,667
Okay.

459
00:19:48,100 --> 00:19:50,567
NCIA will handle our side

460
00:19:50,700 --> 00:19:53,400
and NLEA will handle your side.

461
00:19:53,533 --> 00:19:54,500
But...

462
00:19:55,333 --> 00:19:57,400
once we see just one--

463
00:19:57,533 --> 00:20:00,667
My team will coordinate
with your team.

464
00:20:07,967 --> 00:20:08,900
Thank you.

465
00:20:09,733 --> 00:20:10,700
Alright.

466
00:20:12,467 --> 00:20:13,500
[DOOR OPENS]

467
00:20:13,633 --> 00:20:15,600
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

468
00:20:20,433 --> 00:20:21,500
[MAX] Sir.

469
00:20:23,867 --> 00:20:25,333
I'm Maxine Jacinto.

470
00:20:25,467 --> 00:20:26,467
You are...

471
00:20:27,167 --> 00:20:29,433
General Jacinto's
eldest daughter.

472
00:20:29,567 --> 00:20:30,667
Sam's big sister.

473
00:20:31,600 --> 00:20:34,000
If you find out anything
about the case, please...

474
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:36,967
let me know right away.

475
00:20:39,500 --> 00:20:40,967
You can count on me.

476
00:20:41,100 --> 00:20:42,167
Thank you.

477
00:20:45,200 --> 00:20:46,667
Your sister is a fighter.

478
00:20:48,033 --> 00:20:49,400
I know her well.

479
00:20:51,033 --> 00:20:52,567
As long as she can fight,

480
00:20:53,633 --> 00:20:54,933
she won't give up.

481
00:20:55,833 --> 00:20:57,467
I believe that too.

482
00:21:00,900 --> 00:21:01,933
Take care.

483
00:21:02,067 --> 00:21:04,300
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

484
00:21:04,433 --> 00:21:06,833
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

485
00:21:08,267 --> 00:21:10,367
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

486
00:21:10,500 --> 00:21:11,667
[LINE RINGING]

487
00:21:12,900 --> 00:21:13,967
Yes, General?

488
00:21:14,633 --> 00:21:17,133
Domingo, I want you
to do one more thing.

489
00:21:17,267 --> 00:21:18,733
What is it, sir?

490
00:21:18,867 --> 00:21:20,500
Keep an eye on the Zafras.

491
00:21:20,633 --> 00:21:22,200
<i> Investigate their businesses.</i>

492
00:21:22,333 --> 00:21:24,533
Do your research on them
so we can find...

493
00:21:25,433 --> 00:21:26,733
dirt on them.

494
00:21:26,867 --> 00:21:29,200
I will give orders
to my people immediately.

495
00:21:29,333 --> 00:21:30,533
And, General,

496
00:21:30,667 --> 00:21:33,533
we're round the clock
searching for Samantha.

497
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:35,233
Domingo, my daughter is safe.

498
00:21:35,367 --> 00:21:37,367
But still keep looking for her.

499
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:39,600
<i>However, one of
our priorities right now</i>

500
00:21:39,733 --> 00:21:41,500
is to weaken the Zafras.

501
00:21:42,400 --> 00:21:43,533
<i> We're in a race.</i>

502
00:21:43,667 --> 00:21:45,233
<i> Not just against time,</i>

503
00:21:45,367 --> 00:21:46,767
but also against the enemy.

504
00:21:47,767 --> 00:21:48,833
Yes, General.

505
00:21:48,967 --> 00:21:55,067
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

506
00:21:55,200 --> 00:21:56,667
Sir.

507
00:21:56,800 --> 00:21:58,267
You asked for us?

508
00:21:58,400 --> 00:22:01,333
We have a new assignment
from General Jacinto.

509
00:22:01,467 --> 00:22:02,733
Nice. [SNICKERS]

510
00:22:02,867 --> 00:22:07,267
We're doing a great job so now
he's giving us more work to do.

511
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:08,500
[SNICKERS]

512
00:22:08,633 --> 00:22:10,133
Who's our target, sir?

513
00:22:10,267 --> 00:22:11,767
The Zafras.

514
00:22:11,900 --> 00:22:14,933
I want you to start
with the parents.

515
00:22:15,100 --> 00:22:17,033
Who they talk to,

516
00:22:17,167 --> 00:22:20,100
who they hang with,
and their usual spots.

517
00:22:20,233 --> 00:22:22,033
And also their transactions.

518
00:22:22,167 --> 00:22:23,700
Uh, sir,

519
00:22:23,833 --> 00:22:25,833
are we looking
for something particular?

520
00:22:25,967 --> 00:22:28,000
I know Mariano Zafra.

521
00:22:28,133 --> 00:22:30,733
He used to work for NLEA
but got dismissed.

522
00:22:30,867 --> 00:22:32,733
He had tons
of cases against him.

523
00:22:32,867 --> 00:22:34,733
He doesn't abide by the law.

524
00:22:34,867 --> 00:22:37,600
I'm sure
he has skeletons in the closet.

525
00:22:37,733 --> 00:22:39,033
I want you to investigate them.

526
00:22:41,233 --> 00:22:42,300
Why, sir?

527
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:45,300
What is General Jacinto up to?

528
00:22:46,033 --> 00:22:48,600
The war between the Jacintos
and the Zafras

529
00:22:48,767 --> 00:22:50,667
is just getting started.

530
00:22:52,400 --> 00:22:54,000
Do your wounds still hurt?

531
00:22:54,133 --> 00:22:55,767
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

532
00:22:55,900 --> 00:22:56,800
[OBJECT THUDS]

533
00:22:57,867 --> 00:23:00,533
NLEA is still
a thorn in my side.

534
00:23:01,900 --> 00:23:04,733
I have served there
for many years.

535
00:23:04,867 --> 00:23:08,833
But they still dismissed me
without due process!

536
00:23:08,967 --> 00:23:12,833
And now they're still
ruining my plans!

537
00:23:12,967 --> 00:23:14,067
What's done is done.

538
00:23:15,867 --> 00:23:19,333
Let's not dwell on things
we can't change.

539
00:23:19,467 --> 00:23:21,833
But that opportunity
went to waste.

540
00:23:23,100 --> 00:23:24,633
Victor was with me.

541
00:23:24,767 --> 00:23:26,467
We were going to make it.

542
00:23:26,600 --> 00:23:27,700
What do we do now?

543
00:23:28,700 --> 00:23:30,067
All is not lost.

544
00:23:31,700 --> 00:23:33,267
Pia can still do something.

545
00:23:35,267 --> 00:23:36,967
Seriously?
You believe in that woman?

546
00:23:37,933 --> 00:23:40,933
She couldn't help us!
Has she done something?

547
00:23:41,067 --> 00:23:42,433
Did she even warn us

548
00:23:42,567 --> 00:23:45,333
that the NCIA wouldn't be
the only ones there?!

549
00:23:45,467 --> 00:23:47,500
Did she even mention
the NLEA backing them up?!

550
00:23:56,767 --> 00:23:58,633
- [LINE RINGING]
- [PHONE RINGING]

551
00:24:01,133 --> 00:24:02,233
Hello, ma'am?

552
00:24:02,367 --> 00:24:03,633
You're free tonight, right?

553
00:24:05,867 --> 00:24:06,933
Come over.

554
00:24:07,667 --> 00:24:08,733
I'm on my way.

555
00:24:08,867 --> 00:24:13,967
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

556
00:24:16,333 --> 00:24:22,700
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

557
00:24:29,533 --> 00:24:30,933
[SAM] I have to take action.

558
00:24:31,767 --> 00:24:34,033
<i> I need to find evidence.</i>

559
00:24:38,467 --> 00:24:45,433
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

560
00:24:53,267 --> 00:25:00,133
[MUSIC TURNS STIRRING]

561
00:25:13,300 --> 00:25:16,567
<i>I have to find something.
Anything!</i>

562
00:25:17,533 --> 00:25:20,167
<i>All I need is one piece
of evidence</i>

563
00:25:20,300 --> 00:25:24,167
<i>to prove Gabo has a connection
to the Zafras and to Mr. Chan.</i>

564
00:25:26,233 --> 00:25:33,267
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

565
00:25:35,833 --> 00:25:37,133
[DRAWER SCRAPES]

566
00:25:37,267 --> 00:25:40,300
[OBJECTS CLATTERING]

567
00:25:43,333 --> 00:25:44,733
[DRAWER SCRAPES]

568
00:25:44,867 --> 00:25:47,333
[BOOKS THUDDING]

569
00:25:49,533 --> 00:25:50,500
[DRAWER SHUTS CLOSE]

570
00:25:53,533 --> 00:26:00,500
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

571
00:26:15,567 --> 00:26:22,333
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

572
00:26:22,467 --> 00:26:23,633
[OBJECTS CLATTER]

573
00:26:29,367 --> 00:26:30,567
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

574
00:26:30,700 --> 00:26:34,633
"Statement of Early Release
under Parole"

575
00:26:35,933 --> 00:26:37,833
<i> He was saying the truth.</i>

576
00:26:37,967 --> 00:26:40,367
<i> He was given parole.</i>

577
00:26:41,500 --> 00:26:48,433
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

578
00:26:55,300 --> 00:27:01,667
[MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

579
00:27:01,933 --> 00:27:04,000
<i> I know who you want!</i>

580
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:05,667
<i>- Alright.
- It's a regular, right?</i>

581
00:27:05,800 --> 00:27:07,100
<i> Nikolas, where are you?!</i>

582
00:27:07,233 --> 00:27:09,867
<i>Get my machete!
I'll kill your father!</i>

583
00:27:09,967 --> 00:27:12,933
<i> Kulas! I'll kill you!</i>

584
00:27:13,067 --> 00:27:15,433
<i>You are not doing
your job enough!</i>

585
00:27:15,600 --> 00:27:18,200
<i>I've been looking
for my sister for days.</i>

586
00:27:18,333 --> 00:27:20,600
<i>What have you done
the entire day?</i>

587
00:27:20,733 --> 00:27:22,200
<i>You kept worrying,
you kept crying.</i>

588
00:27:22,333 --> 00:27:24,200
<i> Did that help us? It didn't!</i>

589
00:27:24,333 --> 00:27:25,667
<i> Please forgive me</i>

590
00:27:25,800 --> 00:27:28,800
<i>if I make a mistake
and commit a sin.</i>

591
00:27:28,933 --> 00:27:30,867
<i> I won't do it on purpose.</i>

592
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:33,567
<i>Don't worry, love.
I will prepare for you.</i>

593
00:27:33,700 --> 00:27:36,600
So that when we sleep together,

594
00:27:36,733 --> 00:27:39,600
<i>you will hug
and kiss me yourself.</i>
